WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.963
Every policy, in every
wave, passes the same gates.

2
00:00:03.963 --> 00:00:08.114
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 02 set the durations,

3
00:00:08.114 --> 00:00:12.737
and Microsoft's own minimum is a week
in report-only before enforcement.

4
00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:15.551
Gate one is report-only,
two to four weeks,

5
00:00:15.551 --> 00:00:18.876
while impact, gaps and
exclusions are reviewed.

6
00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:23.537
Gate two is a pilot ring of IT
and security staff for two weeks.

7
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:27.444
Gate three expands ring by
ring, one to two weeks each:

8
00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:32.350
headquarters, then field and remote
staff, then everyone in scope.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.587
Then steady state: enforced,
monitored, with drift alerts.

10
00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:40.412
Inside that, the chapter
consolidates a seven-step cycle.

11
00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:45.352
One, a pre-deployment check: prerequisites
exist, readiness gates are met, the

12
00:00:45.352 --> 00:00:47.469
emergency exclusion is present,

13
00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:51.075
and the policy JSON has been
reviewed in source control.

14
00:00:51.075 --> 00:00:53.912
Two, create the policy in report-only.

15
00:00:53.912 --> 00:00:59.460
One detail: a report-only policy that
requires a compliant device can prompt users

16
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.560
on macOS, iOS and Android
to pick a certificate,

17
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.313
so leave those platforms out
of the report-only version.

18
00:01:06.313 --> 00:01:08.975
Three, measure for at least seven days.

19
00:01:08.975 --> 00:01:12.815
Four, analyze and remediate:
missing registrations,

20
00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:17.637
noncompliant devices, untagged
applications, empty attributes.

21
00:01:17.637 --> 00:01:21.888
Fix the cause; add an exclusion
only as a governed object.

22
00:01:21.888 --> 00:01:25.974
Five, security and business owners
approve the impact analysis,

23
00:01:25.974 --> 00:01:28.826
and that approval is
kept as change evidence.

24
00:01:28.826 --> 00:01:32.125
Six, enforce for the
pilot ring and expand.

25
00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:37.425
Turning a policy that targets all users
straight from off to on is never allowed.

26
00:01:37.425 --> 00:01:40.700
Seven, watch for forty-eight
hours after each ring.

27
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.416
The readiness gates are
the program's numbers:

28
00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:48.063
at least ninety-five percent of in-scope
users have a method that satisfies the

29
00:01:48.063 --> 00:01:51.422
policy's strength, and at
least ninety percent of devices

30
00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:54.925
are enrolled and compliant,
with the attributes populated.

31
00:01:54.925 --> 00:01:59.075
The point is that each wave starts with
a measured number, not an estimate.

32
00:01:59.075 --> 00:02:01.526
And a wave starts only
after the previous one

33
00:02:01.526 --> 00:02:04.220
has been enforced for a
week without an incident.
